// `new T[0]` and a negative count.
//
// A zero-length array used to be allocated as an array of length zero, so every
// index into it was a bounds failure at run time:
//
//     var a = new int[0];
//     a[0] = 1;   // "array index 0 out of bounds (length 0)", exit 134
//
// That is a run-time error about something the reader could have been told
// about while reading the program, and the reader cannot act on it there. Both
// forms are diagnosed at the `new` instead.
int main() {
    var a = new int[0];
    var b = new string[-3];
    return 0;
}
